Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Darkn OS dual boot helper. Run this once in Windows (double-click, then Yes).

; 1) Keep the hardware clock in UTC, like Linux does, so the time stops
;    jumping by hours every time you switch between the two systems.
[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\TimeZoneInformation]
"RealTimeIsUniversal"=dword:00000001

; 2) Turn off Fast Startup. With it on, Windows only hibernates at shutdown
;    and leaves its drives locked, so Linux can open them read-only at best.
[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Session Manager\Power]
"HiberbootEnabled"=dword:00000000
